      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Shadow data\" does not provide a grace period; the GDPR mandates that personal data removal be completed within one calendar month, typically requiring an immediate response from data controllers. If specific scripts or legacy systems prevent immediate deletion, you do not get extra time, but you are permitted a justification for those delays by documenting the specific technical obstacles and providing a remediation plan. There is no interim \"safe harbor\" for data found in unmanaged areas like shadow databases; technically referencing or minimizing data counts as a violation until the removal is technically complete. The most effective defense for your team is to demonstrate a robust data governance policy and a clear roadmap for unlocking or purging all inaccessible legacy systems as quickly as possible after the request is received.",
